-----------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE:
Before running this script make backup from your logs.
This script should not touch the QSO data itself, but
security first!

If you have checked 'save log data to local machine' checkbox
simplest way is to save folder ~/.config/cqrlog to the safe place.
If something goes wrong first delete ~/.config/cqrlog from HD and then
restore ~/.config/cqrlog from the safe place back to your HD.

Keep Cqrlog closed while doing these.
-----------------------------------------------------------------


For updating QRZlog logid numbers to old qsos that you
have saved to QRZlog before you upgraded to version (142)
[or higher] that supports QRZlog online logs upload.
(preferences/Online logs/QRZlog).

You must first download QRZlog as adif file from QRZ.com
'logname' is 'cqrlogXXX'
 where XXX is 3digit zero padded log number like 001

Use: ./idupdate.sh <adif_file_name> <logname> [> /tmp/debug.txt]

Start Cqrlog before running script if you have
checked 'save log data to local machine' checkbox.
Keep Cqrlog running while this script runs!

Otherwise check script variable 'sqlcmd' to correspond
your SQL server settings and cqrlog database log number.
You do not need to start Cqrlog in that case.

You can direct output to debug text file adding arrow right
followed by filename to the end of srcipt starting command line.

